Fidetype trust guarantee sheet
==============================
config_id            tcfg-8fa3866deec917f3
input                logits (custom:fidetype.pretrained.lmreadout.LmReadout.decode_fn.<locals>.gated_lm_readout)
guarantee            P( wrong-commit rate <= 0.05 ) >= 0.9
                     wrong-commit rate = wrong COMMITs / all utterances
method               Learn then Test, exact binomial p-values, fixed-sequence grid 1.00 -> 0.00 step 0.01, combined with the policy-grid threshold by max
calibration items    106 = 26 fit + 40 policy grid + 40 LTT
LTT items needed     >= 45 LTT items (utterances, not commits) to certify any COMMIT
lambda_hat           inf (feasible: False)
commit threshold     p_top1 >= never commits (no threshold certified)
commit gate          {"max_guard_risk": 1.0, "min_chars": 1, "min_words": 0}
LTT items (in-sample) 0 commits, 0 wrong (of 40; 0 blocked by the commit gate; median guard risk 0.097873)
null controls        pass if commits <= floor(0.05 x n)
  uniform            0/300 commits (allowed 15): PASS
  shuffled           0/300 commits (allowed 15): PASS
  user               0/106 commits (allowed 5): PASS
assumptions
  - Exchangeable data: the calibration utterances and the live utterances come from the same distribution (same user, device, decoder, task and session type). Use a random sample, not a hand-picked one.
  - The decoder, its weights, the vocabulary and the decode settings do not change after calibration.
  - The true texts are right, and they use the same text normalisation as the decoder output (the wrapper joins runs of spaces and strips the ends; nothing else).
  - Each utterance is decided once (no repeats), and the calibration items were used for nothing else.
not guaranteed
  - Any single utterance: the bound is on the rate over many utterances.
  - A bound per session, per user or per sentence type: the bound is on the mix of the calibration data.
  - Data that differ from the calibration data (a new day, a new electrode position, a new user, drift).
  - The error rate among commits (precision): with few commits it can be high.
  - The quality of offered choices, or how often the guard commits (it may commit rarely or never).
  - Correctness of the text that the guard withholds or offers.
  - Any medical or legal claim. Fidetype is research software, not a medical device.
warnings
  ! only 40 LTT items (< 45): no threshold can be certified, so the guard never commits. Give more labelled utterances.
  ! frame temperature not fitted (1.0): with your own decode_fn, pass stream_texts= (the truth in the decoder's token space) to fit it. The guarantee does not depend on it.
  ! the guard never commits (no certified threshold). It still offers and withholds.
